{"authored" [{"question" "q-49354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{5x+7}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7 \\\\  & ↓ & -10 \\\\  & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+7}{x+2}=5-\\frac{3}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x+7}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5-\\frac{3}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\text{d}x-3\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8e91c02ba20fbea134c908e328151703f7c74397295a2b0d8d666d753e26a5" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5x+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{x+4}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 \\\\  & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+4}{x+3}=1+\\frac{1}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{x+4}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(1+\\frac{1}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{|}_{-2}^{0}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =(0-(-2))+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-2+3|) \\\\  & =2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8e91c02ba20fbea134c908e328151703f7c74397295a2b0d8d666d753e26a5" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 3 & 3 & -9 & 1 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & 9 & 0 & 3 \\\\  & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}=3{x}^{2}+1+\\frac{2}{x-3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+1+\\frac{2}{x-3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8e91c02ba20fbea134c908e328151703f7c74397295a2b0d8d666d753e26a5" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-3x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "407237fd73cf938032bb77e814fe127bf0a6214db423d7e16a5e44349598b8ef" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 \\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/example-485.json" "file_sha256" "ef188c4641dbce7d6568c40e3f7f7b217143010192f8f5b32fe89235efa21dcf" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}-1$ | $4$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1} = 4 -\\dfrac{5}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4-\\frac{5}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x{|}_{0}^{1}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[4-0]-5[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1] \\\\  & =4-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/example-485.json" "file_sha256" "ef188c4641dbce7d6568c40e3f7f7b217143010192f8f5b32fe89235efa21dcf" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-486" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{2x^2-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/example-486.json" "file_sha256" "f3bd8b3c13b9c88abdc940a44368c9addd9ad1b2eac275b00090df5f1d4c70df" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-486" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division. \n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^2$ | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}3$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n|  | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{ 2x^2-3x-4}{x-3} = 2x + 3 + \\dfrac {5}{x-3} .\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+3+\\frac{5}{x-3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+3x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/example-486.json" "file_sha256" "f3bd8b3c13b9c88abdc940a44368c9addd9ad1b2eac275b00090df5f1d4c70df" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/example-487.json" "file_sha256" "74cc433dc6e312bb5f45b15cb080b8b7ff7c6fb7a9326388395de2dc44daf0bc" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x-1}{2(x-\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}\\dfrac12$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $\\dfrac12$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-\\dfrac12$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} & =1-\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\frac{1}{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/example-487.json" "file_sha256" "74cc433dc6e312bb5f45b15cb080b8b7ff7c6fb7a9326388395de2dc44daf0bc" "basis" 1540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-49411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3x-2}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 \\\\  & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x-2}{x+1}=3-\\frac{5}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x-2}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3-\\frac{5}{x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804"} {"question" "q-49411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C"] ["math" "3x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C"] ["math" "3x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C"] ["math" "3x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C"] ["math" "3x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{5x+7}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7 \\\\  & ↓ & -10 \\\\  & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+7}{x+2}=5-\\frac{3}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x+7}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5-\\frac{3}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\text{d}x-3\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "5x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "5x+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "5x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{9x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $9$ | $7$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-36$ |\n|  | $9$ | $-29$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{9x+7}{x+4}=9-\\frac{29}{x+4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{9x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}(9-\\frac{29}{x+4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\text{d}x-29{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9x\\,{|}_{-1}^{2}-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|\\,{|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =9(2-(-1))-29(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-1+4|) \\\\  & =27-29(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =27-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{6}{3}) \\\\  & =27-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,2\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804"} {"question" "q-352220" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352220" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "27"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352220" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352220" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{8x+1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,23\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $8$ | $1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-24$ |\n|  | $8$ | $-23$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{8x+1}{x+3}=8-\\frac{23}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{8x+1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}(8-\\frac{23}{x+3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\text{d}x-23{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8x\\,{|}_{2}^{4}-23\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|\\,{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =8(4-2)-23(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+3|) \\\\  & =16-23(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5) \\\\  & =16-23\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{7}{5}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804"} {"question" "q-352219" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352219" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "16"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352219" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352219" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{x+4}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 \\\\  & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+4}{x+3}=1+\\frac{1}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{x+4}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(1+\\frac{1}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{|}_{-2}^{0}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =(0-(-2))+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-2+3|) \\\\  & =2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] ["math" "-3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] ["math" "2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] ["math" "3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $-7$ | $5$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $3$ | $-4$ | $1$ |\n|  | $3$ | $-4$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}=3{x}^{2}-4x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-4x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{|}_{1}^{2}-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2}+x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}{|}_{1}^{2}-2{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2}+x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[{2}^{3}-{1}^{3}]-2[{2}^{2}-{1}^{2}]+[2-1] \\\\  & =7\\cdot 1-2(3)+1 \\\\  & =7-6+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804"} {"question" "q-352247" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352247" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{2}+7x+10}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -5 & 1 & 7 & 10 \\\\  & ↓ & -5 & -10 \\\\  & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+7x+10}{x+5}=x+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{2}+7x+10}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1}+2x{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}]+2[1-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804"} {"question" "q-49457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "-\\frac{4}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡6"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 3 & 3 & -9 & 1 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & 9 & 0 & 3 \\\\  & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}=3{x}^{2}+1+\\frac{2}{x-3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+1+\\frac{2}{x-3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-3x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $1$ | $8$ | $7$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-4$ | $-16$ |\n|  | $1$ | $4$ | $-9$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}=x+4-\\frac{9}{x+4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x+4-\\frac{9}{x+4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}x-9{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{3}+4x\\,{|}_{0}^{3}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|\\,{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{2}-{0}^{2})+4(3-0)-9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3+4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+4|) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}+12-9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{2}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{7}{4}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{33}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-6}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & 3 & -6 \\\\  & ↓ & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\  & 1 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-6}{x-2}={x}^{2}+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-6}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}+3)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+3x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804"} {"question" "q-49460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+3x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-6x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}x-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+3x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{x+1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $4$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x+1}{4(x+\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4} & 1 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & 1 & \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{4})} & =1+\\frac{(\\frac{3}{4})}{(x+\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{3}{4(x+\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{3}{4x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int (1+\\frac{3}{4x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\int \\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[x+\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{3}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804"} {"question" "q-49357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{3}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C"] ["math" "x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C"] ["math" "x-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-49357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{3}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-73390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{8x-1}{4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-73390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $4$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8x-1}{4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8x-1}{4(x-\\frac{3}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{8x-1}{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & 8 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & 6 \\\\  & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x-1}{(x-\\frac{3}{4})} & =8+\\frac{5}{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8x-1}{4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int (8+\\frac{5}{x-\\frac{3}{4}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8\\int \\text{d}x+5\\int \\frac{1}{x-\\frac{3}{4}}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|]+C \\\\  & =2x+\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-73390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804"} {"question" "q-73390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-73390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x+\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C"] ["math" "2x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C"] ["math" "x+\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-73390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x+\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-358987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{7}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-358987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $3$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3(x-2/3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{(x-2/3)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $4$ | $-5$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $\\frac{8}{3}$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-\\frac{7}{3}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x-5}{(x-2/3)} & =4-\\frac{(7/3)}{(x-2/3)} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{7}{3x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(4-\\frac{7}{3x-2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[4{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\text{d}x-7{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[4x-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[4(3-1)-\\frac{7}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[8-\\frac{7\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{7}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-358987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804"} {"question" "q-358987" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-358987" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-358987" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-358987" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-358835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-3}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{11}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-358835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-3}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-3}{2(x+1/2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-3}{(x+1/2)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $5$ | $-3$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-\\frac{5}{2}$ |\n|  | $5$ | $-\\frac{11}{2}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-3}{(x+1/2)} & =5-\\frac{(11/2)}{(x+1/2)} \\\\  & =5-\\frac{11}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-3}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(5-\\frac{11}{2x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x-11{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[5x-\\frac{11}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5(1-0)-\\frac{11}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5-\\frac{11\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{11}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-358835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804"} {"question" "q-358835" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-358835" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-358835" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-358835" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-114896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-114896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $6$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6(x+\\frac{1}{6})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & 2 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & 2 & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})} & =2+\\frac{(\\frac{2}{3})}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{4}{6x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}(2+\\frac{4}{6x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[2x+\\frac{4}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+1|]}_{-1/12}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[2x+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+1|]}_{-1/12}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2(0-(-\\frac{1}{12}))+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6(0)+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6(-\\frac{1}{12})+1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2(\\frac{1}{12})+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-114896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804"} {"question" "q-114896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-114896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{16}(1+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{16}(3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{25}(5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{36}(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "q-114896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "27a94b2295a19440a6c25f6ac39c54f4b2fc6f5f364b38bbdc1c44758ac37e4b"} {"question" "e-485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 \\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/example-485.json" "file_sha256" "b42c58115e743587337e33fc8f314c96ba32226dbaffa01dea973002c679ecb5"} {"question" "e-485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}-1$ | $4$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1} = 4 -\\dfrac{5}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4-\\frac{5}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x{|}_{0}^{1}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[4-0]-5[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1] \\\\  & =4-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/example-485.json" "file_sha256" "b42c58115e743587337e33fc8f314c96ba32226dbaffa01dea973002c679ecb5"} {"question" "e-486" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{2x^2-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/example-486.json" "file_sha256" "2369e892c94f0510d2b99450d6c4e78debb441225306586a61babf8196ad23b0"} {"question" "e-486" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division. \n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^2$ | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}3$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n|  | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{ 2x^2-3x-4}{x-3} = 2x + 3 + \\dfrac {5}{x-3} .\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+3+\\frac{5}{x-3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+3x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/example-486.json" "file_sha256" "2369e892c94f0510d2b99450d6c4e78debb441225306586a61babf8196ad23b0"} {"question" "e-487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/example-487.json" "file_sha256" "c1e99b781722bdd13842d9d823e0af98a2776fe4e00042ecd3021830408aae98"} {"question" "e-487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x-1}{2(x-\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}\\dfrac12$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $\\dfrac12$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-\\dfrac12$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} & =1-\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\frac{1}{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/example-487.json" "file_sha256" "c1e99b781722bdd13842d9d823e0af98a2776fe4e00042ecd3021830408aae98"}] "usage" {"q-49456" [] "q-49398" [] "e-486" [] "q-49354" [] "e-485" [] "e-487" []} "basis" 1750 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186314906 17592186314907 17592186314908 17592186314909 17592186314910 17592186314913 17592186314914 17592186314915 17592186314916 17592186314917 17592186314934 17592186314935 17592186314936 17592186314937 17592186314938] "immutable_fields" [[17592186314905 :answer-field/correct] [17592186314905 :answer-field/id] [17592186314905 :answer-field/key] [17592186314905 :answer-field/type] [17592186314912 :answer-field/correct] [17592186314912 :answer-field/id] [17592186314912 :answer-field/key] [17592186314912 :answer-field/type] [17592186314933 :answer-field/correct] [17592186314933 :answer-field/id] [17592186314933 :answer-field/key] [17592186314933 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
